From a0ab5e0387d4bfc27df7015103996043da33b11d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tonka <tonkatriathlete@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 21:09:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hermes-agent): add nearby_prospect behavior

First Hermes advisory behavior, built end-to-end against the agent API.

- pure core (proximity.ts): haversine distance, drop-in time-window gate,
  eligibility (un-visited or high-priority), ranking, suggestion payload
- HTTP client (client.ts): Bearer-auth wrapper over /api/agent/*
- orchestrator (nearby-prospect.ts): anchor = rep's most recent visit's
  business coords; rank nearby eligible prospects; post cards; report run
- CLI runner (run-nearby.ts) for the scheduled harness
- tests: 15 unit tests over the pure core + a deterministic live e2e driver

Defaults: 1.0 mi radius, 09:00-17:00 America/Chicago, max 3 cards/run.
Dedupe key hermes:nearby:{repId}:{businessId}:{date} (upsert, never stacks).
